      "content": "A lack of nutrients can definitely contribute to yellowing leaves, especially if the plant isn't receiving enough essential micronutrients like magnesium or iron. However, Monstera deliciosa typically thrives in low-nutrient conditions, so it's unlikely that your plant is lacking essential nutrients like nitrogen. Instead, you might consider adjusting your watering schedule to allow the soil to dry out slightly between waterings, as this can help prevent root rot.",
